California laws, regulations, and official state guidance relevant to AI and robotics in clinical trials
California generally does not replace federal FDA oversight for investigational drugs/devices, but it does impose independent human subject protection duties, health information confidentiality requirements, and certain AI-specific healthcare communications constraints that frequently affect oncology trial sites, sponsors, and vendors operating in California. [9]
