U.S. federal laws, regulations, and official agency guidance relevant to AI and robotics in clinical trials
The federal framework is dominated by FDA authority over drugs/biologics/devices and by human subject protection/privacy regimes that apply depending on funding, institutional commitments, and data custody. For AI/robotics in oncology trials, the most common “directly binding” rules are FDA regulations for IND/IDE and human subject protections (21 CFR Parts 312/812/50/56), plus HIPAA (where applicable) and electronic records controls (21 CFR Part 11). [31]
